    "type": "question",
    "label": "59",
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $x$ in terms of $a$ and $b$.\n$$x^2-6abx+a^2(9b^2-4a^2)=0.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=3ab\\pm2a^2$.\n\nComplete the square to obtain $(x-3ab)^2=4a^4$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-6abx+9a^2b^2-4a^4&=0\\\\(x-3ab)^2-4a^4&=0\\\\(x-3ab)^2&=4a^4\\\\x-3ab&=\\pm2a^2\\\\x&=3ab\\pm2a^2.\\end{align*}$$\nThese coincide when $a=0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
